tion"} [:p {} "Heavily favoured in this event was Austria’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/55175"} "Franz Aigner"] ", the reigning World Champion. Some competition was expected from the Baltic athletes, notably " [:a {:href "/athletes/67356"} "Harald Tammer"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/56293"} "Kārlis Leilands"] ". But, as in the " [:a {:href "/results/28565"} "featherweight"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/28613"} "middleweight"] ", an Italian lifter proved stronger than the favorites. " [:a {:href "/athletes/56155"} "Giuseppe Tonani"] ", who had competed in " [:a {:href "/results/21134"} "tug-of-war at the 1920 Olympics"] ", proved to be evenly matched with Aigner, finishing equal in three of the five events."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Behind these two, the competition for bronze was also close. Three competitors — Tammer, Leilands, and Frenchman " [:a {:href "/athletes/55648"} "Louis Dannoux"] " — finished " [:em {} "ex aequo"] " with 497.5 kg. The tie was resolved with a “lift-off” in the double-handed clean &amp; jerk, which Tammer won with 142.5 kg, ahead of Dannoux with 140. It is not known if Leilands also participated in the tie-break."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Kilograms"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/56155"} "Giuseppe Tonani"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "517.5"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/55175"} "Franz Aigner"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amaz